WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.158
The sun rose, and the children were no longer statues.

2
00:00:09.159 --> 00:00:13.064
They were standing knee-deep in brambles and grass.

3
00:00:13.065 --> 00:00:19.244
The lawn, the marble steps, and the pool had disappeared.

4
00:00:19.245 --> 00:00:21.448
It was very cold.

5
00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:24.825
"We're on the island," said Mabel.

6
00:00:24.826 --> 00:00:26.801
"But we can't swim anymore.

7
00:00:26.802 --> 00:00:29.877
We're stuck here."

8
00:00:29.878 --> 00:00:35.635
"Isn't there a boat somewhere?" Jimmy asked.

9
00:00:35.636 --> 00:00:39.709
"No." Mabel shivered.

10
00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:44.289
"There must be something we can do," said Gerald.

11
00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.449
"The ring!" cried Mabel.

12
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.429
"We can wish ourselves home.

13
00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.328
Do you have the ring, Kathleen?"

14
00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:55.397
Kathleen shook her head.

15
00:00:55.398 --> 00:00:58.648
"Psyche wanted to see it so I gave it to her.

16
00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:04.149
It's probably still on her finger!"

17
00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:07.883
Everyone tried not to be angry with Kathleen.

18
00:01:07.884 --> 00:01:12.710
But everyone was upset.

19
00:01:12.711 --> 00:01:18.594
"Maybe we can find Psyche's statue and get the ring back," said Gerald.

20
00:01:18.595 --> 00:01:22.637
"I've never seen that statue," said Mabel.

21
00:01:22.638 --> 00:01:25.723
Kathleen sniffled.

22
00:01:25.724 --> 00:01:28.558
She was about to cry.

23
00:01:28.559 --> 00:01:32.675
"Why don't we explore the island," said Gerald.

24
00:01:32.676 --> 00:01:36.937
"Maybe we'll find a boat."

25
00:01:36.938 --> 00:01:41.657
None of them believed that they'd find a boat.

26
00:01:41.658 --> 00:01:45.953
But they set off to explore the island anyway.

27
00:01:45.954 --> 00:01:48.708
They were all miserable.

28
00:01:48.709 --> 00:01:52.794
The brambles scratched Mabel's bare feet and legs.

29
00:01:52.795 --> 00:01:57.038
She had left her shoes and stockings on the mainland.

30
00:01:57.039 --> 00:02:01.174
"Come on, everybody, cheer up," said Gerald.

31
00:02:01.175 --> 00:02:03.705
"We'll get out of here."

32
00:02:03.706 --> 00:02:08.510
Suddenly he stumbled and disappeared with a yell.

33
00:02:08.511 --> 00:02:11.540
Mabel nearly fell too.

34
00:02:11.541 --> 00:02:16.734
Right in front of her was a flight of moss-covered steps.

35
00:02:16.735 --> 00:02:22.045
"Gerald, are you hurt?" she called down the steps.

36
00:02:22.046 --> 00:02:28.456
"A little," he said. "But I found a passage."

37
00:02:28.457 --> 00:02:33.868
"There's always a passage in this place," said Jimmy.

38
00:02:33.869 --> 00:02:39.459
"I forgot about that passage!" declared Mabel.

39
00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:44.734
"It goes under the water and comes out at the Temple of Flora!

40
00:02:44.735 --> 00:02:50.729
Maybe it even goes past the place where the Ugly-Wugly found his good hotel."

41
00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:55.650
"I'm not going down there in the dark," said Kathleen.

42
00:02:55.651 --> 00:02:59.052
Gerald came back up the steps.

43
00:02:59.053 --> 00:03:02.506
"Maybe there's a secret spring."

44
00:03:02.507 --> 00:03:07.602
Then Gerald led the way down the steps.

45
00:03:07.603 --> 00:03:12.012
He held Kathleen's hand so she wouldn't feel afraid.

46
00:03:12.013 --> 00:03:16.379
The steps led to a passage, which took a turn.

47
00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.712
Then there were more steps.

48
00:03:18.713 --> 00:03:24.362
These led to a straight, clean, marble passage.

49
00:03:24.363 --> 00:03:28.976
Suddenly the children found themselves in a great hall.

50
00:03:28.977 --> 00:03:31.425
The room was filled with light.

51
00:03:31.426 --> 00:03:36.240
And each one of them noticed something different in the arches around the room.

52
00:03:36.241 --> 00:03:38.049
There was a ship at sea.

53
00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:39.771
A king on his throne.

54
00:03:39.772 --> 00:03:44.654
The Ugly-Wugly sitting happily in front of a good hotel.

55
00:03:44.655 --> 00:03:50.041
"Oh, I'm glad we came!" said Kathleen.

56
00:03:50.042 --> 00:03:53.464
They walked slowly through the hall.

57
00:03:53.465 --> 00:03:57.341
At the end of the hall, they saw the source of the light:

58
00:03:57.342 --> 00:03:59.790
the statue of Psyche.

59
00:03:59.791 --> 00:04:05.666
On its hand was the ring.

60
00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:10.648
"I hope you don't mind," Gerald said to the statue.

61
00:04:10.649 --> 00:04:15.551
He removed the ring very gently.

62
00:04:15.552 --> 00:04:21.833
They passed Psyche and entered a dark, twisting passage.

63
00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:25.323
"Give me the ring, Gerald," said Kathleen.

64
00:04:25.324 --> 00:04:28.123
"I know what to say."

65
00:04:28.124 --> 00:04:33.961
Gerald handed it to her reluctantly.

66
00:04:33.962 --> 00:04:39.983
"I wish," she said slowly, "that no one at home will know we've been out tonight.

67
00:04:39.984 --> 00:04:47.444
I wish we were safe in our own beds and asleep."

68
00:04:47.445 --> 00:04:58.751
And that is exactly what happened next.

